@page "/scroll-area"

<PageTitle>Scroll Area · Bheadless</PageTitle>

<div class="bb-intro">
    <h1>Scroll Area</h1>
    <p class="bb-subtitle">Native scrolling with custom scrollbars you can style. The content scrolls as in any scrolling element - keyboard, wheel, touch, screen readers, find in page - while thumbs, overflow hooks and fade variables are kept up to date in the browser, with no .NET call per scroll.</p>
</div>

<SectionSwitcher Slug="scroll-area" />

<DemoBlock Title="Vertical list"
           Code="@_listCode"
           Css="@_listCss">
    <Description>
        <code>BitBhScrollAreaViewport</code> is the native scroll container, its own scrollbars hidden;
        <code>BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar</code> + <code>BitBhScrollAreaThumb</code> draw the custom one. With the default
        <code>Type="Hover"</code> the scrollbar shows while the pointer is over the area or the content scrolls
        (<code>data-state="visible"</code>), and hides <code>ScrollHideDelay</code> (600 ms) after the pointer leaves - fade it
        with <code>[data-state="hidden"]</code>. Drag the thumb, press the track to page, or use the wheel over it. The list has
        nothing focusable, so the viewport itself becomes a tab stop while it overflows: focus it and scroll with the arrow
        keys. Its <code>role="region"</code> and <code>aria-label</code> say what it is.
    </Description>
    <LiveContent>
        <BitBhScrollArea class="scroll-area">
            <BitBhScrollAreaViewport class="scroll-area-viewport" role="region" aria-label="Release tags">
                <div class="scroll-area-content">
                    <p class="scroll-area-heading">Tags</p>
                    @foreach (var tag in tags)
                    {
                        <div class="scroll-area-tag">@tag</div>
                    }
                </div>
            </BitBhScrollAreaViewport>
            <BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar class="scroll-area-scrollbar">
                <BitBhScrollAreaThumb class="scroll-area-thumb" />
            </BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar>
        </BitBhScrollArea>
    </LiveContent>
</DemoBlock>

<DemoBlock Title="Both axes and the corner"
           Code="@_bothCode"
           Css="@_bothCss">
    <Description>
        One scrollbar per axis: <code>Orientation="BitBhOrientation.Horizontal"</code> lays a scrollbar along the bottom.
        <code>Type="Always"</code> keeps both visible, overflow or not. Where they meet, <code>BitBhScrollAreaCorner</code>
        fills the square - sized from the scrollbars through <code>--bit-bh-scroll-area-corner-width</code> /
        <code>-height</code>, which the scrollbars also stop short of. Thumb lengths follow the visible fraction
        (<code>--bit-bh-scroll-area-thumb-height</code> / <code>-width</code>, at least 18px).
    </Description>
    <LiveContent>
        <BitBhScrollArea Type="BitBhScrollAreaType.Always" class="scroll-area scroll-area-wide">
            <BitBhScrollAreaViewport class="scroll-area-viewport" role="region" aria-label="Build log">
                <pre class="scroll-area-log">@log</pre>
            </BitBhScrollAreaViewport>
            <BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar class="scroll-area-scrollbar">
                <BitBhScrollAreaThumb class="scroll-area-thumb" />
            </BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar>
            <BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar Orientation="BitBhOrientation.Horizontal" class="scroll-area-scrollbar">
                <BitBhScrollAreaThumb class="scroll-area-thumb" />
            </BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar>
            <BitBhScrollAreaCorner class="scroll-area-corner" />
        </BitBhScrollArea>
    </LiveContent>
</DemoBlock>

<DemoBlock Title="Fading edges, shown while scrolling"
           Code="@_fadeCode"
           Css="@_fadeCss">
    <Description>
        <code>Type="Scroll"</code> shows the scrollbar while the content scrolls (and while the pointer is on it), then hides
        it <code>ScrollHideDelay</code> later - 900 ms here. The root carries <code>--bit-bh-scroll-area-overflow-y-start</code>
        / <code>-end</code>: the pixels of content hidden past each edge. A mask that fades over <code>min(2.5rem, …)</code>
        of them fades an edge only where there is more to see, and no further than there is. <code>data-overflow-y-start</code>
        / <code>-end</code> (and <code>data-scrolling</code>, <code>data-hovering</code>) are there for selectors.
    </Description>
    <LiveContent>
        <BitBhScrollArea Type="BitBhScrollAreaType.Scroll" ScrollHideDelay="900" class="scroll-area scroll-area-faded">
            <BitBhScrollAreaViewport class="scroll-area-viewport" role="region" aria-label="Terms of service">
                <div class="scroll-area-content">
                    @foreach (var paragraph in paragraphs)
                    {
                        <p class="scroll-area-paragraph">@paragraph</p>
                    }
                </div>
            </BitBhScrollAreaViewport>
            <BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar class="scroll-area-scrollbar">
                <BitBhScrollAreaThumb class="scroll-area-thumb" />
            </BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar>
        </BitBhScrollArea>
    </LiveContent>
</DemoBlock>

<DemoBlock Title="Focusable content, right to left"
           Code="@_rtlCode"
           Css="@_rtlCss">
    <Description>
        A row of filter chips scrolls sideways. The chips take the focus, so the viewport stays out of the tab order (the
        browser scrolls a focused chip into view). <code>Dir="BitBhDirection.Rtl"</code> (or a
        <code>BitBhDirectionProvider</code>) writes <code>dir</code> on the root: the content starts on the right, the thumb
        moves right to left and a vertical scrollbar would sit on the left. <code>Type="Auto"</code> shows the scrollbar
        whenever the content overflows.
    </Description>
    <LiveContent>
        <div class="scroll-area-demo">
            <BitBhScrollArea Dir="BitBhDirection.Rtl" Type="BitBhScrollAreaType.Auto" class="scroll-area scroll-area-strip">
                <BitBhScrollAreaViewport class="scroll-area-viewport" role="region" aria-label="Filters">
                    <div class="scroll-area-chips">
                        @foreach (var filter in filters)
                        {
                            <button type="button" class="scroll-area-chip" aria-pressed="@(selected.Contains(filter) ? "true" : "false")"
                                    @onclick="() => Toggle(filter)">@filter</button>
                        }
                    </div>
                </BitBhScrollAreaViewport>
                <BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar Orientation="BitBhOrientation.Horizontal" class="scroll-area-scrollbar">
                    <BitBhScrollAreaThumb class="scroll-area-thumb" />
                </BitBhScrollAreaScrollbar>
            </BitBhScrollArea>
            <p class="scroll-area-output">Filters: <strong>@(selected.Count == 0 ? "none" : string.Join(", ", selected))</strong></p>
        </div>
    </LiveContent>
</DemoBlock>

